========================================================================
(2)+(3) the n*=9 parity law: VACUOUS at n=18 (debt always present)
========================================================================
   n=18, n*=9: of 3000 primitive 17-sets, FULL-SUPPORT debt-free (parity fires): 0
   => the parity obstruction is VACUOUS for primitive sets at n=18.
   3-adic reason: mod 9 nonzero residues split into UNITS (v3=0: {1,2,4,5,7,8})
   and v3=1 multiples-of-3 ({3,6}). A v3=1 runner can contribute 0 mod 9 (c=3,6);
   a UNIT runner contributes all of {1..8}. So with any unit runner, 0 is
   reachable -> debt present. Debt-free needs ALL runners divisible by 3 =>
   recurse to the n=6 mod-3 law one level down => non-primitive. Prime-power recursion.

   PARITY-FIRING DEGRADATION vs n (fraction of primitive sets that are debt-free):
   n   n*  phi(n*)  units mod n*               parity-fires?
    4   2    1    [1]                       240/400
    6   3    2    [1, 2]                    12/400
    8   4    2    [1, 3]                    0/400
    9   9    6    [1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 8]        0/400
   10   5    4    [1, 2, 3, 4]              0/400
   12   6    2    [1, 5]                    0/400
   14   7    6    [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]        0/400
   16   8    4    [1, 3, 5, 7]              0/400
   18   9    6    [1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 8]        0/400
   => parity fires often only at n=4 (n*=2, units {1}); rare at n=6 (n*=3);
      VANISHES once n* has >=2 units AND a non-unit-nonzero residue (n>=8-ish).

========================================================================
(4) CASCADE heuristic (S527): threshold passes for n=18 (margin 2.58)
========================================================================
   n=7: (n-1)((n-2)/n)^(n-2) = 1.1156  (>=1 => cascade passes)
   n=14: (n-1)((n-2)/n)^(n-2) = 2.0445  (>=1 => cascade passes)
   n=16: (n-1)((n-2)/n)^(n-2) = 2.3132  (>=1 => cascade passes)
   n=18: (n-1)((n-2)/n)^(n-2) = 2.5823  (>=1 => cascade passes)
   AP=regular-18gon: feasible measure after each runner -> final=0.00000 (EMPTIES (tight))
      chain (every 3rd): [0.889, 0.704, 0.483, 0.31, 0.106, 0.022]
   random primitive: feasible measure after each runner -> final=0.14826 (stays >0 (lonely))
      chain (every 3rd): [0.889, 0.641, 0.469, 0.315, 0.219, 0.158]
   NON-RIGOROUS: the (n-2)/n per-step shrink needs a discrepancy bound
   (Erdos-Turan); its log factor is exactly what keeps n=18 open.

========================================================================
(5) HONEST VERDICT
========================================================================
   PROVEN (rigorous) for n=18:
     - no-multiple-of-q case for each q<=18 (t=1/q lonely); strongest single class
       q=9 (t=1/9). A counterexample must be q-covered for ALL q in {2..18}.
   CHARACTERIZED (new, this session):
     - the n*=9 parity law is VACUOUS for primitive sets: inside debt is ALWAYS
       present. The 'free parity' that settled half of n=4 contributes NOTHING at
       n=18 because 9=3^2 has 6 units + a 3-adic sublevel. Debt-free recurses to the
       n=6 mod-3 law one 3-adic level down (non-primitive). Prime-power degradation.
   HEURISTIC (non-rigorous):
     - cascade threshold passes with margin 2.58; the AP (regular 18-gon) is tight
       (carve empties to 0); all sampled primitive sets stay lonely.
   NOT PROVEN: the fully-sieve-covered residual with the discrepancy/coupling gap --
     the same wall as n=14/16 and the general conjecture. n=18 is NOT proved here.
